Test data

tests.archive
    An archive written from docs/FORMAT.md and checked on Multics MR12.8
    (2026-09-22): ac t and ac tl listed it without error, and its SHA-256
    matched after a base64 transfer. Besides some ordinary text
    components, it holds a set of small archives with deliberately bad
    headers (t_badmode, t_baddate, t_bigbc, t_trailing, t_unaligned,
    t_obsolete, t_nofence), one with a left-justified bit count
    (t_leftbc), one with a 32-character component name (t_longname), and
    a good one (t_ok). Its other components are the Multics programs that
    were used to run the same cases on Multics.

tests.ac_t.txt, tests.ac_tl.txt
    The output of ac t and ac tl for tests.archive on Multics. The tests
    require archive t and archive tl to print the same thing, apart from
    the pathname in the title.

The two-digit-year tests in 01-read.t use clock values returned by
convert_date_to_binary_ on Multics MR12.8.

bound_secure_hash_.dense9
    bound_secure_hash_.archive from Multics (2026-09-24), exported with
    encode_base64 -dense9, header line removed and base64 decoded: a raw
    dense9 archive of 207,000 bits (5,750 words). Components: the object
    segments secure_hash_ (127,080 bits) and sha256 (70,200 bits), with
    9th bits set, and the bindfile bound_secure_hash_.bind (7,002 bits).
